# MODULE 6: DATA TYPES AND RELATIONSHIPS

## PART A: SALESFORCE DATA TYPES

Data Types define what kind of information a field can store.

| Data Type | Meaning | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Text | Stores normal text. | Rahul |
| Text Area | Stores multiple lines of text. | Address |
| Number | Stores numeric values. | 100 |
| Currency | Stores monetary values. | ₹50,000 |
| Percent | Stores percentage values. | 75% |
| Checkbox | Stores True or False. | Active / Inactive |
| Date | Stores a date. | 10-11-2026 |
| Date/Time | Stores date and time. | 10-11-2026 10:30 AM |
| Email | Stores email addresses. | test@gmail.com |
| Phone | Stores phone numbers. | 9876543210 |
| URL | Stores website links. | www.google.com |
| Picklist | Allows selection of one predefined value. | Male / Female |
| Multi-Select Picklist | Allows multiple predefined values. | Java, Python |
| Auto Number | Automatically generates sequential numbers. | AUD-001 |
| Formula | Calculates values automatically. | Quantity × Price |
| Roll-Up Summary | Summarizes related child records. | Total Amount |
| Geolocation | Stores latitude and longitude. | Location coordinates |
| Time | Stores time values. | 10:30 AM |

### Important Data Types

**1. Auto Number**

Automatically generates a unique sequential number.

Example:
- STU-001
- STU-002
- STU-003

**2. Formula**

Automatically calculates a value based on other fields.

Example:

Total Price = Quantity × Unit Price.

Users cannot manually edit the calculated value.

**3. Roll-Up Summary**

Calculates information from related child records and displays it on the parent record.

Example:

A customer has five orders. A Roll-Up Summary can calculate the total value of those orders.

**4. Picklist**

Allows users to select one value from a predefined list.

Example:

Status:
- New
- In Progress
- Completed

**5. Checkbox**

Stores either True or False.

Example:
- Active = True
- Inactive = False

