# SUGGESTED PRACTICAL LEARNING ORDER

Complete these exercises in your Salesforce Developer Org or Trailhead Playground.

1. Create a custom Student object.
2. Create Name, Age, Email and Phone fields.
3. Create a custom tab for the Student object.
4. Create five Student records.
5. Create a College object.
6. Establish a Lookup Relationship between Student and College.
7. Create another object and practice a Master-Detail Relationship.
8. Import sample records using Data Import Wizard.
9. Create a List View and apply filters.
10. Create a Compact Layout.
11. Customize a Record Page using Lightning App Builder.
12. Create a Quick Action.
13. Create a Formula Field.
14. Create a Roll-Up Summary Field.
15. Create a Validation Rule.
16. Create a Report.
17. Practice Tabular, Summary and Matrix Reports.
18. Create a Dashboard using your report.
19. Configure Profiles and Permission Sets.
20. Practice OWD, Role Hierarchy and Sharing Rules.
21. Explore In-App Guidance and create a Prompt.

**Final Learning Tip:** Do not just memorize the definitions. Create the objects, fields, records and relationships yourself. Salesforce is much easier to understand when you practice each concept in a Playground.
